# Goal: etude-8u3 — populate run-worktree submodules and record their SHAs

BUILD. The premise is confirmed in current source: `worktree.Checkout` stops after
`git worktree add --detach`, the Go tree has no submodule population path, and live
runs pass that empty checkout directly to stage and gate-check runners.

## Design

1. Extend `worktree.Checkout` to run `git submodule update --init --recursive --checkout`
   in the detached run worktree before returning it. Linked worktrees use the
   superproject's shared common `.git/modules` repositories, so subsequent runs reuse
   fetched submodule objects rather than cloning a fresh object database per run. If
   population or enumeration fails, remove the partially-created worktree and prune its
   registration before returning a contextual error.
2. Enumerate every populated submodule recursively after update, recording its Git
   display path and resolved `HEAD` OID on the returned `Worktree`. Use NUL-delimited
   output so spaces in paths are not ambiguous.
3. Add an optional `submodules` path-to-OID map beside each stage's `git_sha` in the run
   manifest wire format. Treat it as an additive leaf (legacy manifests omit it), copy
   the checkout map into every live-run stage, preserve it through JSON round trips, and
   validate that paths are clean relative Git paths and values are full lowercase 40- or
   64-character OIDs.
4. Thread the one checkout snapshot through fresh and resumed live-run execution. The
   same immutable gitlink pins apply to every stage, so every stage records the same map.
5. Update the shipped manifest documentation to explain that repo-state identity is the
   superproject `git_sha` plus the optional recursive `submodules` map.

