## Verification

Planned regression: `TestCheckoutPopulatesPinnedSubmoduleAndReusesObjectStore` creates a
real local submodule, advances its source after the superproject pins the first commit,
checks out the superproject, reads the pinned content, verifies the resolved SHA, and
confirms linked checkouts share the superproject module object store.

Planned regression: `TestEngineRunCheckReadsPinnedSubmoduleAndManifestRecordsSHA` creates
a throwaway superproject with a real submodule plus an executable gate check that prints
and compares the file inside it. A live run must pass the real check, its recorded raw
check output must equal the pinned content, and the stage manifest must map the submodule
path to the pinned SHA rather than the newer source HEAD.

Planned regression: manifest JSON round-trip and validation cases cover omission for
legacy/no-submodule stages, preservation of multiple recursive entries, invalid paths,
and invalid OIDs.

Run `go test ./internal/worktree ./internal/runmanifest ./internal/liverun`, then
`make test`, `make lint`, `make docs-reality`, and `make docs-check`. This is not a new
CLI surface, so no installed-binary manual CLI matrix is required; the live engine test
is the required behavioral proof.

## Scope and safety

ANCESTOR: etude-8u3 (P1) — fix the observed empty-submodule checkout defect and make
repo-state reproducible; measurement is the reported 40/0 false-failure incident and the
current zero Go-source submodule handling sites.

BLAST RADIUS: the repository's shared Git module-object cache and disposable run
worktrees only; no host packages, services, credentials, containers, or external writes.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCES: none

TOPOLOGY: concurrent disposable linked worktrees share the superproject common Git dir
and its module repositories; nested submodules are recursively populated and enumerated.

DURABILITY CLASS: population is an idempotent at-least-once local cache fill; the durable
stage manifest records the AUTHORITATIVE checked-out submodule HEAD values pinned by the
superproject gitlinks.

COMPLETENESS ENUMERATION: all worktree consumers use the one Checkout population point;
all live-run manifest stages use the one runAndCaptureStage construction point; add,
update, and enumeration failures all fail closed and clean the disposable checkout.

TRUST BOUNDARY: repository-controlled `.gitmodules` and gitlinks are consumed by Git;
paths are not interpolated into an authored shell command, Git verifies object identity,
and the manifest rejects non-clean paths or non-full lowercase OIDs.

Rejected alternative: record only the gitlink OIDs from the superproject tree without
populating submodules. That would identify content checks still cannot read and fails the
behavioral acceptance. Rejected alternative: clone each submodule into every temporary
worktree with an isolated object store; linked-worktree Git already provides a shared
common module store and avoids that repeated cost.
